<!--
  Padded copy of `ic_tool_scanner` used **only** by the after-call screen's
  tool grid.

  The shared `ic_tool_scanner.xml` is a 24×24 vector whose artwork fills the
  viewport edge-to-edge. In the after-call grid this made the scanner glyph
  read as ~50 % larger than the other tool icons (which all come from the
  `ic_action_*` 512×512 family, where the artwork only fills ~55 % of the
  viewport).

  This file widens the viewport to 44×44 and wraps the original path in a
  centring `<group>`. The drawing itself is identical — only the empty
  margin around it grew, so when `fitCenter` scales the asset into the
  32 sdp icon slot it visually matches Merge / Split / Compress.

  The original `ic_tool_scanner.xml` is kept untouched for all other call
  sites in the app (home screen tools, scanner activity headers, etc.).
-->
